{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1525082-how-would-this-\u2018build\u2019-do-in-combat","id":1525082,"title":"How would this \u2018build\u2019 do in combat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-05T11:02:23-08:00","id":1525082,"title":"How would this \u2018build\u2019 do in combat?","content":"I have no experience yet with the mechanics of 3rd edition since I\u2019m yet to get a group for it running and I\u2019d like some insight in how effective my character would be.<br /> <br /> I am thinking of a off-tank/dodge tank character that uses Laughing Monster Style, solar dodge and the Gnomon artifact to get initiative from dodging and proc counterattacks from Laughing Monster Style. Laughing monster will also soft force some opponents to focus me or face a penalty. Gnomon is there for the intitiative order manipulation effects and I\u2019m tempted to throw in a gem of perfect mobility as well for that one more dexterity action.<br /> <br /> The character is not fully specialized in combat so I\u2019ll start out with laughing monster up and including the form,<br /> dodge charms until the charm that forces the opponent to lose iniative on dodge and only the first evocation of Gnomon and (if I take it) gem of mobility.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m adding the awakened eye JB adder (I hate that it\u2019s based on perception -_-) to enhance the chances of pricing Gnomon and getting a decent initiative pool to start from. <br /> <br /> Finally I was thinking of mists of Eventide because it\u2019s both good for combat as well good for my larceny adventures.<br /> <br /> My questions are:<br /> <br /> 1 Would the above be a good enough build to face starting level threats in Ex3 and would it scale well enough later?<br /> <br /> The character will be a larceny supernal so later the disarming part of the build can compliment Laughing Monster. <br /> <br /> 2 are there any fun things I could incorporate into the build that are in the same themes of stealing initiative, sabotage gambits and breaking action economy?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27166-reficulris","name":"Reficulris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T16:51:31-08:00","id":1525096,"title":"","content":"A Solar character with Dexterity 3, Combat Ability 4, and an Excellency is good enough to face starting level threats. The amount of combat stuff you're considering taking would make you a primary combatant, starting the game fully capable of fighting <i>end</i> level threats as a support character or mid level threats in the spotlight.<br /> A heavy focus on action economy shenanigans will massively amplify this - you've pinpointed options with exceptionally good synergy. Your starting PC is likely to be able to fare excellently in a fight against <i>anything</i>, even if you never buy another combat Charm.<br /> As a side note, Gnomon is dangerously good - if any part of your character is banned at a given table, it's probably Gnomon. Mists is a pretty close second.<br /> <br /> For further funtimes:<br /> Brawl 3 opens up Thunderclap Rush Attack, which lets you completely disregard the Initiative order.<br /> Poised Lion Attitude (in Miracles of the Solar Exalted) lets you make reflexive social influence attempts, which is always good.<br /> Subtle Speech Method helps you antagonize people (thus meeting your form's reflexive activation condition) without antagonizing the wrong people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T10:03:24-08:00","id":1525126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1525082-how-would-this-\u2018build\u2019-do-in-combat?p=1525096#post1525096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Solar character with Dexterity 3, Combat Ability 4, and an Excellency is good enough to face starting level threats. The amount of combat stuff you're considering taking would make you a primary combatant, starting the game fully capable of fighting <i>end</i> level threats as a support character or mid level threats in the spotlight.<br /> A heavy focus on action economy shenanigans will massively amplify this - you've pinpointed options with exceptionally good synergy. Your starting PC is likely to be able to fare excellently in a fight against <i>anything</i>, even if you never buy another combat Charm.<br /> As a side note, Gnomon is dangerously good - if any part of your character is banned at a given table, it's probably Gnomon. Mists is a pretty close second.<br /> <br /> For further funtimes:<br /> Brawl 3 opens up Thunderclap Rush Attack, which lets you completely disregard the Initiative order.<br /> Poised Lion Attitude (in Miracles of the Solar Exalted) lets you make reflexive social influence attempts, which is always good.<br /> Subtle Speech Method helps you antagonize people (thus meeting your form's reflexive activation condition) without antagonizing the wrong people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the comprehensive answer!<br /> <br /> I thought I would be more on the weak side of the equation but I\u2019m coming from 2.5 and more used to paranoia combat and such meaning a lot of upfront combat investments being necessary.<br /> <br /> I love the suggestions, thunderclap rush attack seems very powerful and fitting and brawl 3 is only 2 dots more then the m.a. prerequisite of brawl 1 anyway! The two social charms are very juicy too!<br /> <br /> Gnomon being so good it gets banned would be sad because a lot of the character leans on it. Maybe I\u2019ll talk with my storyteller to see if it fits his vision and/or needs to be adjusted.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27166-reficulris","name":"Reficulris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}